72-## 2. Catalog Invariants
73-
74-1. Examples are **structure-first**.
75-2. Examples provide **response geometry**, not reasoning authority.
76-3. Examples do not define reasoning policy.
77-4. Examples do not include selection rules.
78-5. Each entry is independent and does not claim priority over other entries.
79-6. Each entry must include at least:
80-   - `task_family`
81-   - `structure_type`
82-   - `context_contract`
83-   - `expected_sections`
84-   - `verification_pattern`
85-   - `risk_profile`
86-   - `anti_patterns`
87-   - `generalization_boundary`
88:   - `example_body`
89-7. Examples must never replace user-provided facts.
90-8. Examples must never waive external evidence requirements.
91-9. Examples must never remove approval requirements for high-risk work.
92-10. Examples must never hold execution control.
93-11. Example bodies may include placeholders, but may not include runtime decision authority.
94-12. Advanced prompting examples remain **family exemplars**, not activation owners.
95-13. Multimodal examples remain **artifact shape exemplars**, not modality-policy owners.
96-14. Judge/evaluation artifacts remain **report shapes**, not evaluation authority.
97-15. Chaining-shaped examples remain **artifact shapes**, not execution-loop owners.
98-16. Routing-shaped examples remain **decision memo shapes**, not router policy owners.
99-17. Parallelization-shaped examples remain **fan-out / join artifact shapes**, not concurrency owners.
